When utilizing pseudo-labeling for a target domain, we propose using multiple translations of the same target image to generate more reliable pseudo-targets. By assuming that these translations represent the target domain's diversity, our approach averages their predictions to produce a better pseudo-target. Experimental results on the benchmarks "mindcloud-15" and "mindcloud-20" demonstrate that our method achieves superior pseudo-targets compared to other techniques, ultimately leading to enhanced domain adaptation performance. The code for our approach has been made available on GitHub at the specified URL. Additionally, our method's section provides further details. 

